KG42.register("clusters-5d13696805e6aef7cd7a7cc2",{"id":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v142-d-K001","paper":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction","label":"Admission, solicitation, and conditional response for next-hour electricity bids","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Admission, solicitation, and conditional response for next-hour electricity bids","market_meaning":"With available generation units, the estimated next-hour demand, and floor-price information as inputs, the aggregator solicits bids from registered agents, the DER agents perform the initial participation decision, and the aggregator collects available power and prices. When supply exceeds demand, the price-reduction request and the agents' continued bidding or exit constitute a conditional response. This cluster is limited to bid interaction and does not claim to have determined termination conditions, clearing outcomes, or optimal procurement.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","bidding","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Each chain belongs to the same hourly mechanism of the grid-connected microgrid. The initial floor-price comparison and the subsequent price-reduction response apply separately; the correct estimation of demand is a given assumption, and the product chain limits the transaction object. The correspondence of floor-price parameters is limited to the initial comparison for the same DER and the same hour and does not extend to round-by-round prices or the clearing price.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Registration, demand announcement, price announcement, bid response, and bid receipt jointly form a procedural rule with clear inputs and bid outputs. The boundary is determined on the basis of actual information exchange and response conditions; supplier eligibility, final pricing, and power-supply allocation are assembled separately.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Provides the registration prerequisite for bid interaction; it is displayed in association with registration statements in other chains and is not counted as another set of admission rules."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the input activity in which the aggregator announces the next-hour demand to registered agents."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides solicitation, initial submission or exit, and the bid response after price reduction."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Completes the receiving-side activity in which bids are delivered to the aggregator and collected; lowest cost is retained only as a verbal objective."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the initial electricity-price announcement and the price-reduction request when supply exceeds demand."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplements the agents' participation decision and the source of floor-price information; the initial submission decision overlapping with R003 is not counted as an independent rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"context","rationale":"Limits the bid object to the electricity provided by grid-connected DERs for the next-hour centralized load, and does not add a product dependency edge on this basis."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e001"],"rationale":"The registration requirement and the supply-bid prerequisite target the same set of available microgrid generation units, forming an interface between admission activity and bid activity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e001"],"rationale":"The two chains encode the same registration threshold respectively as a procedural requirement and as participation logic, retaining their expressive differences and adding no independent admission obligation."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16"],"rationale":"Algorithm 1 combines the next-hour demand announcement and the solicitation of bids from registered agents as aggregator interaction, and the demand announcement provides the procurement context for that solicitation."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E17"],"rationale":"The initial utility-grid floor-price announcement corresponds to the initial submission decision, and the price-reduction request after excess supply corresponds to the re-bidding response; the two signal uses remain distinguished by branch."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e002"],"rationale":"The submission and exit branches of R003 together correspond to the initial binary-decision encoding of R009; a single branch is not equated with the complete decision, and this comparison is not extended to all re-bidding rounds."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17"],"rationale":"Solicitation and continued bidding produce bids sent to the aggregator, and R005 supplements the activity of receiving available power and prices in the bids."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L07","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17"],"rationale":"The source explicitly connects bid collection, the supply-demand check, and the price-reduction request under excess supply, supporting the collection result as the information source for the conditional judgment; no supply-demand formula is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L08","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E17"],"rationale":"The re-bidding request after price reduction and the exit of agents that have lost interest from that hour's auction belong to the same conditional response, and no numerical exit formula that could replace the interest judgment is given."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L09","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"The product description limits the commodity whose bids are collected, the next-hour time domain, and the centralized-load use; it only supplements the transaction scope and does not turn background explanation into a new necessary condition."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L10","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-der-base-price","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-utility-base-price"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::theta::theta_p_base_der","v141-c-R009::theta::theta_p_base_util"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e002"],"rationale":"The two chains use the DER floor price and the utility-grid floor price in the initial comparison of Algorithm 1 respectively from the perspectives of supply submission and participation decision; the parameters correspond by category and retain their local roles."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::admission.local_area","v141-c-R003::V::admission.local_area","v141-c-R009::V::admission.local_area"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::admission.local_area","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e001"],"rationale":"The three frozen references are all used for the registration admission function of the same mechanism; the representative item is used only for display, and registration is not interpreted as an additional geographical eligibility requirement."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R009::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16"],"rationale":"These references all point to the DER aggregator function that organizes the same hourly auction; merging the displayed subject references does not merge their different activities or scientific edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17"],"rationale":"The three are the sending, collection, and conditional-response perspectives of the same supply-submission function; they are not thereby taken to imply that bids or supply quantities in different rounds are equal."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R009::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E17"],"rationale":"Only identifies the same price-coordination function node in the frozen directory. The DER private floor price, the utility-grid floor price, and round-by-round announcements play different roles; the context of each reference is retained, and no assertion is made that the price quantities are the same."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-der-base-price","v141-c-R009::theta::theta_p_base_der"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e002"],"rationale":"In the initial participation comparison for the same DER and the same hour, the two parameters point to that agent's floor-price input; the local parameter objects for the supply judgment and the participation judgment are both retained and are not generalized as identities across subjects or across hours."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-utility-base-price","v141-c-R009::theta::theta_p_base_util"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e002"],"rationale":"The two parameters correspond to the utility-grid floor price in the initial comparison for the same hour, not to subsequent reduced auction bids or the final clearing price; the parameter roles in each chain are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-M07","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e001"],"rationale":"The three center on the same registration threshold and are expressed respectively as a unary procedural obligation, a supply prerequisite, and participation logic. The differences in expressive strength and encoding are left for checking and are not regarded as three independent admission requirements."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B evidence used remains unverified and has only experimental candidate-use eligibility. The provenance of j, the price symbols, and formalization_origin in C has also not undergone independent review; assembled only means that assembly is possible within the above procedural scope.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e001","v141-b-g02-e002"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the references, local formalization, and all assembly mappings item by item against the original text; this round does not rewrite source status and does not claim that the scientific content has undergone independent review."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G02","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Yellow-pages registration is carried by admission.local_area, but directory registration is not automatically equivalent to geographical admission eligibility. The directory node proposal has still not been approved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::admission.local_area","v141-c-R003::V::admission.local_area","v141-c-R009::V::admission.local_area"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e001"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P01"],"required_work":"Check the compatibility of the registration function with the existing admission definition; if extension is needed, the proposal should be handled upstream, and for now only the frozen reference is retained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G03","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The price-coordination node carries both private floor-price information and aggregator announcements. The j description in R009 concerns the current round, but the explicit criterion of C004 is limited to the initial comparison; the conversion from cost or SOC to floor price, the round-by-round prices, and the exit criterion are not closed by these chains. The example price reduction cannot be directly upgraded to a general rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R009::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R009::x::x_join_decision","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C004","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e020"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P03","proposal:v141-b-g02-p01"],"required_work":"Retain the distinctions among the various prices and between initial and re-bidding rounds; if an executable iterative model is needed, check back with the source to clarify the roles of quantities, the rounds, and the exit conditions, and handle the not-yet-approved price node proposal upstream."}]},"rule_refs":["15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R001","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R002","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R003","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R005","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R006","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R009","15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R011"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-143910e2088c2223","COMP-334f35169e6933ed","COMP-536dedc5bf0853eb","COMP-790cb7aca96f4d38","COMP-97d6b21fedc8f7d3","COMP-a1af16dd42f1ff08","COMP-b646a091517c6af0"]});
